        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"project_id\": \"{{project_id}}\",\n  \"email\": \"new.person@example.com\",\n  \"role\": \"member\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/functions/v1/send-invite-email",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "functions",
            "v1",
            "send-invite-email"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "description": "Sends an invitation email through the deployed Supabase Edge Function.\n\nBefore using this request, deploy send-invite-email from Dashboard → Edge Functions → Deploy a new function → Via Editor. Paste the complete source from supabase/functions/send-invite-email/index.ts. The function uses Gmail SMTP at smtp.gmail.com:465 automatically. Add only SMTP_USER (Gmail address), SMTP_PASSWORD (Google App Password), and optional SMTP_FROM under Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets.\n\nThe caller must be signed in and authorized as a project owner/admin. The invitee does not need an existing Auth account. Only an owner can invite someone as admin.\n\nSet frontend_origin to the frontend URL (e.g. http://localhost:3000). Postman sends it as Origin; browsers send Origin automatically. The function accepts valid HTTP/HTTPS origins during development; restrict this before production.\n\nPOST {{base_url}}/functions/v1/send-invite-email\nBody: project_id, email, and optional role (admin/member/viewer; defaults to member). The raw invitation token is emailed and is never returned in the response."
    },
